From 8f43da3a5f4791c009111135d35535cab44e88f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Gleason <alex@alexgleason.me>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:27:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Sign through a local NIP-5F signer (nostrd) when it holds the
 account

When a signer listens on ~/.local/share/nostr/signer.sock (or
nostr.signer-socket), ngit signs, and encrypts with NIP-44, through it
for the account it would otherwise sign as: the one --signer or
nostr.signer selects, or the signer's active account when none is
selected. It needs neither the key nor a bunker connection. Accounts the
signer doesn't hold, and keys or bunkers given on the command line, are
signed for as before. nostr.signer-socket=false turns it off.

Account management (login, logout, export-keys), which asks for a
config scope, still sees ngit's own credentials.
